British actor Tom Ellis is having one  hell of a time playing the lead role in  TVs Lucifer a police procedural which  follows the devil himself as he retires  to the City of Angels and teams up with  LAPD detective Chloe Decker  so with Lucifer back on our screens  let's take a look at seven crazy facts  about the devilish show Tom Ellis may  play the former Lord of hell and Lucifer  but in real life he actually grew up in  a very religious family Ellis's father  was a Baptist pastor as his Ellis's  sister brother-in-law and uncle and when  they heard he was making this show they  were very excited for him  Ellis says he sees the show Lucifer as a  satirical story of redemption rather  than a big theological debate well  before the show had even aired it was  already the target of protests with  several organizations petitioning the  show's Network Fox to counsel a series  completely a petition on the American  family Association's website one Million  Moms which gathered 38,000 signatures  said the show mischaracterized and  glorified Satan and that if Fox went  ahead with their plans to Lucifer the  network would be disrespecting  Christianity and mocking the Bible this  isn't the first time the world of  Lucifer's caused controversy though or  the Neil Gaiman's Sandman graphic novel  which the TV show is loosely based on  along with the spin-off comic Lucifer  also drew fire from the American Family  Association back in 1991 not only is a  series inspired anti Lucifer protests  it's also inspired Pro Lucifer graffiti  yes in keeping with the show's devilish  spirit someone in LA or perhaps more  than one person took it upon themselves  to spray-paint the words watch Lucifer  on top of billboards advertising other  network shows such as NBC's shades of  blue and they even added a set of horns  to act as heads featuring on those  billboards including Jennifer Lopez Tom  Alice's steady doesn't know who did it  and he doesn't condone it but he does  find it very funny when author Neil  Gaiman created the character of Lucifer  and the Sandman graphic novels he was  inspired by David Bowie however after  reading the show scripts Tom Ellis saw  Lucifer as an Oscar Wilde or no coward  character with added rock-and-roll  spirit so he approached Lucifer as if  the character were the love child of  Noel Coward and Mick Jagger with a dash  of British actor terry-thomas the TV  shows still tips its hat to Bowie's  influence on the  books though by featuring his music as  for choosing Lucifer's accent  according to Ellis when he tries an  American accent the character came off  as a jerk but with an English accent he  found that Lucifer could get away with  saying all sorts of terrible things and  still come across as rather charming as  music is such a big part of the show  what with Lucifer running a nightclub  and singing and playing the piano  Ellis decided to make a special playlist  for his character which he listened to  during his downtime to help him get into  the part his playlist features a mix of  tracks that appear in the series such as  David Bowie's Fame and rebel rebel as  well as Ellis's own picks including  Purple Haze by Jimi Hendrix and Ring of  Fire by Johnny Cash  Lucifer's showrunner Joe Henderson has  even been known to listen to Alice's  playlist while writing scripts for the  show in fact Devil's hair cut by Beck  was actually on Alice's playlist before  it made it into the show's pilot episode  by the way Ellis comes from quite a  musical family himself his mother was a  music teacher his dad did amateur  operatic and all his siblings grew up  playing instruments with Ellis playing  trumpet and then French horn in  orchestras during his teenage years when  Tricia Helfer was cast as Lucifer's  mother Charlotte for the show's second  season Tom Ellis was blown away as not  only is he a massive Battlestar  Gallactica fan but he also used to have  a crush on the Canadian actress who  played number six in the award-winning  sci-fi series in fact although Helfer  plays Lucifer's mother in the show in  real life she's just four years older  than Ellis and she's actually five years  younger than DB Woodside who plays her  other on-screen son amenadiel Alice's  joke that it's all a bit weird and  oedipal and that he and DB both feel  like Stifler from the American Pie  movies while they were filming at Long  Beach for season one 7th episode wingman  the shoot was repeatedly interrupted by  a random drone flying around the cast  and crew  eventually the show security tracked  down the guy who was flying the drone  but he refused to stop so actor TV  Woodside marched down the beach to  confront the drone pilots who then tried  to make a speedy getaway in his car as  Woodside knocked on his door asking to  speak with him he was only later that  Woodside realized he'd been dressed in  his full amenadiel costume at the time  so guys what are you most enjoying about  the new season of Lucifer and what's  been your favorite part of the show  so far if you enjoyed this video do  comment like and hit that subscribe  button and before you head off you might  also like to watch my video with Tom  Ellis at Comic Con click here to check  that out and you can also click here for  my full movie and TV facts playlist with  more videos like this thanks for  watching and see you next time  yippee-ki-yay movie lovers
 

